---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Portico" description="A personal media server for the movies, shows, music, and live TV you keep.">
  <section class="home-hero">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <h1>Your media, at home on every screen.</h1>
      <p>Portico organizes the movies, shows, music, audiobooks, and live TV on your server and keeps them ready for the people you share them with.</p>
      <div class="hero-links">
        <a class="button button-primary" href="/download/">Download Portico</a>
        <a class="text-action" href="/features/">See what it does <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-product" aria-label="Portico home screen">
      <img src="/media/portico-home.png" alt="Portico home screen showing a personal media library" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="product-section section-light">
    <div class="section-heading split-heading">
      <h2>One server. A full household.</h2>
      <p>Everyone gets their own place to watch. The server owner keeps control of the library, access, and playback.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="product-proof">
      <div class="feature-list">
        <article>
          <h3>Bring the library you already have</h3>
          <p>Add movies, television, anime, music, audiobooks, and live channels without moving the files into someone else's cloud.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Keep each account personal</h3>
          <p>Progress, Saved items, history, ratings, and library access stay with the person watching.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Plays the best way for each screen</h3>
          <p>Portico uses the original file when a device supports it and prepares another stream when it does not.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <figure class="product-image">
        <img src="/media/portico-detail.png" alt="Portico television show detail page" />
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="screen-section">
    <div class="section-heading split-heading">
      <h2>Built for the screen in front of you.</h2>
      <p>Portico uses the same server and account across the web, phones, tablets, televisions, and streaming devices.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="screen-list">
      <div><strong>Web</strong><span>Browse, watch, and manage a server from a desktop browser.</span></div>
      <div><strong>Mobile</strong><span>Take your library and watch progress with you.</span></div>
      <div><strong>TV</strong><span>A remote-first experience built around artwork and playback.</span></div>
      <div><strong>Server</strong><span>Run Portico on Windows, macOS, Linux, or Docker.</span></div>
    </div>
    <a class="button button-secondary" href="/download/">See all downloads</a>
  </section>

  <section class="ownership-section section-light">
    <div class="ownership-copy">
      <h2>The server stays in charge.</h2>
      <p>Your Portico Server owns the library, permissions, and playback. Your Portico Account finds the servers you can use. Private media travels directly between your server and your screen.</p>
      <a class="text-action dark" href="/docs/remote/how-portico-connects/">How Portico connects <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
    <div class="connection-diagram" aria-label="Apps connect directly to a Portico Server">
      <div class="connection-node app-node">
        <div class="device-marks" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 32 32"><rect x="3" y="7" width="18" height="13" rx="1" /><path d="M9 25h6M12 20v5" /></svg>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 32 32"><rect x="9" y="3" width="14" height="25" rx="2" /><path d="M14 24h4" /></svg>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 32 32"><rect x="3" y="6" width="26" height="17" rx="1" /><path d="M11 28h10M16 23v5" /></svg>
        </div>
        <strong>Your apps</strong><span>Web · phone · TV</span>
      </div>
      <div class="connection-path" aria-hidden="true">
        <span>Direct connection</span>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 180 24"><path d="M2 12h176M166 3l12 9-12 9" /></svg>
      </div>
      <div class="connection-node server-node">
        <svg class="server-mark" viewBox="0 0 48 48" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="7" y="7" width="34" height="13" rx="2" /><rect x="7" y="28" width="34" height="13" rx="2" /><path d="M13 13h2M13 34h2M21 13h14M21 34h14" /></svg>
        <strong>Your server</strong><span>Media · access · playback</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="docs-promo">
    <div class="section-heading split-heading">
      <h2>Documentation for setup, watching, and server care.</h2>
      <p>Portico documentation covers the first installation through long-term server maintenance.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="docs-promo-grid">
      <a href="/docs/start/"><strong>Start here</strong><span>Set up a server and add the first library.</span></a>
      <a href="/docs/media/"><strong>Organize media</strong><span>Name files, build libraries, and correct matches.</span></a>
      <a href="/docs/remote/"><strong>Remote access</strong><span>Connect securely when you are away from home.</span></a>
      <a href="/docs/troubleshooting/"><strong>Troubleshooting</strong><span>Work through connection, playback, and library problems.</span></a>
    </div>
    <a class="button button-primary" href="/docs/">Browse documentation</a>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
